   "note": "THE 1786/1851 TANGLE IS BOTH-RIGHT, not a conflict. Title page leaf 11: 'THE NEW-YORK DIRECTORY, CONTAINING, A Valuable and well Calculated ALMANACK ... BY DAVID FRANKS. NEW-YORK: Printed by SHEPARD KOLLOCK, corner of Wall and Water Streets, M, DCC, LXXX, VI.' -- and then, below a rule, 'REPUBLISHED BY JOHN DOGGETT Jr., 59 LIBERTY STREET, NEW YORK, 1851.' The WORK is Franks' 1786 directory; 1851 is Doggett's facsimile reprint. The catalog's 1786 is right about the work and phase 0b's 1851 is right about the artefact. Confirms the plan's note on the fran/_0 pair, with a different reprint house and date. NOTE THE DATE FORM: the original year is set in ROMAN NUMERALS (M, DCC, LXXX, VI), which YEAR_DIGITS cannot see at all -- a fourth attestation channel alongside digits, spelled-out words and the regnal formula."
  },
